## 3. DEPENDENCY & HALLUCINATION GOVERNANCE

### 3.1 Hallucination Gate v2
Every external function, library, API, or framework call must be listed.

| Confidence | Definition | Action |
|------------|------------|--------|
| **CERTAIN** | Standard library of the target language, OR verified against official documentation in this session, OR used successfully in this project with passing tests | Use directly |
| **UNCERTAIN** | Third-party library, new API version, OR not verified in this session | Must have CERTAIN fallback; if no fallback, BLOCK |
| **BLOCKED** | UNCERTAIN + no CERTAIN fallback + no user approval | Code containing this dependency is BLOCKED |

**Resolution Path for BLOCKED:**
1. Propose CERTAIN fallback to user.
2. If user approves UNCERTAIN, document in dependency_audit.md with justification and risk acceptance.
3. If neither, HALT: unresolved UNCERTAIN dependency.

### 3.2 Dependency Audit Artifact (dependency_audit.md)
```markdown
| Name | Version | Path | Confidence | Justification | Fallback | Uncertainty |
|------|---------|------|------------|---------------|----------|-------------|
```
Plus a BLOCKED table if any exist.

