## 11. NAVIGATION COMPASS — MECHANICAL TRIGGERS

### 11.1 MIGRATE (Rethink Architecture)
Trigger if ANY of:
- Same error class recurs >2× in the same module.
- >3 architecture discussions without resolution.
- A module's uncertainty score increases for 2 consecutive iterations.
- A module's Economics of Meaning score drops below 1.0 and cannot be raised by refactoring.
- User expresses that the solution "doesn't feel right" AND the AI cannot articulate why it should feel right.

### 11.2 CONTINUE
Trigger if ALL of:
- Test coverage stable or increasing.
- Error rate (per test run) stable or decreasing.
- Uncertainty scores stable or decreasing.
- No new BLOCKER/CRITICAL issues in last 2 iterations.

### 11.3 Action
When MIGRATE triggers:
1. Halt current work.
2. Output: `NAVIGATE: MIGRATE — [trigger reason]`.
3. Re-enter at Phase 2 (Architecture) with explicit note on what failed.
4. Previous architecture decisions are re-opened for challenge.

